        "listName":  "Kei Ling Ha (Former Sea Crossing Point of the Secret Rescue Operation)",
        "paras":  [
                      "There were two main land routes in the Secret Rescue Operation: the eastern route and the western route. The eastern route ran from Hong Kong Island to Kowloon, then to Ngau Chi Wan and finally to Sai Kung, crossing the sea at Kei Ling Ha to Shayuchong on the opposite shore. On New Year\u0027s Day 1942, Liao Chengzhi, Lian Guan, Qiao Guanhua and other leaders of the Chinese Communist Party, who were to clear the way for the rescue operation, left first. They were escorted to the Kowloon urban area by Li Jianxing, a guerrilla member. Early the next morning, escorted by Huang Guanfang\u0027s Armed Working Team, they disguised themselves as pilgrims, mixed with crowds of refugees and left the city. At Ngau Chi Wan, they met up with Jiang Shui\u0027s Pistol Squad and hurried on to Sai Kung without stopping. Finally, guerrilla member Cai Guoliang escorted them to the cove at Kei Ling Ha. At 3 a.m., Liao Chengzhi and the others arrived at Shayuchong."
                  ]
