                      "On 15 December 1941, Huang Guanfang of the Guangdong People\u0027s Anti-Japanese Guerrilla Force led the Armed Working Team into Sai Kung, and Shan Liu Village became their first foothold in Sai Kung. The ancestral hall of the Wong family in the village was where the guerrillas gathered at that time. Using Shan Liu Village as its base, the Armed Working Team sent members to many places in Kowloon to meet and receive anti-Japanese cultural figures.",
                      "On 1 January 1942, the Armed Working Team and Wong Ya-yuen, the village head of Shan Liu Village, received Liao Chengzhi, Lian Guan, Qiao Guanhua and other leaders of the Chinese Communist Party in the village. The Armed Working Team then escorted them to Kei Ling Ha, where they took a boat to Shayuchong. The team also rescued Lieutenant Colonel Lindsay T. Ride of the British Army and his party, moving them first to Shan Liu Village and then to Ngong Wo Village, so that they escaped the Japanese search for them."
