                      "During the War of Resistance, the villagers of Ngong Wo Village eagerly supported the operations of the Hong Kong-Kowloon Brigade. The family of Ling Niang, the \"Mother of the Guerrilla Force\", gave the guerrillas strong support. Her house stood on the highest ground in Ngong Wo Village, which made it easy to watch the surrounding area. There was also a dense forest behind it, so the Japanese troops did not dare to go there on their sweeps. For a time, her house therefore served as the base of the Brigade\u0027s Quartermaster General\u0027s Office."
