        "paras":  [
                      "According to Ou Weiming, Adjutant of the Quartermaster General\u0027s Office of the Hong Kong-Kowloon Brigade, the guerrillas built cavern storehouses in both Ngong Wo Village and Pak Tam Village. The Quartermaster General\u0027s Office used them to keep supplies, to store weapons, ammunition and money, and as hiding places and shelters. The cavern storehouse in Ngong Wo Village was in the forest on the hill behind the home of Ling Niang, the \"Mother of the Guerrilla Force\". The cavern storehouse, a little over 10 square metres in size, was where the Quartermaster General\u0027s Office kept its supplies and where people hid during the Japanese \"sweep operations\". Ling Niang also helped to build it."
                  ]
