        "listName":  "High Island (Former Operation Base of the Marine Detachment of the Hong Kong-Kowloon Brigade)",
        "paras":  [
                      "During the Japanese Occupation of Hong Kong, Sai Kung was the base area of the Hong Kong-Kowloon Brigade, and the Marine Detachment set up an operation base on High Island. The guerrillas called High Island the \"military port\" because it was the harbour for their fleet of armed boats. Groups escorting renowned cultural figures to the home front (the unoccupied areas of China) also stopped at High Island. The Marine Detachment was very active in these waters. It sabotaged Japanese transport and supply lines and escorted merchants and travellers at sea. The guerrillas lived side by side with the villagers and fishermen. They helped them solve their food problems, set up a primary school for fishermen\u0027s children and formed a fishermen\u0027s association, among other work. The Japanese troops learnt of the maritime guerrillas\u0027 activities and twice sent boats to search for them. However, the fishermen tipped off the guerrillas and actively covered for them, so the Japanese troops returned empty-handed."
                  ]
