        "listName":  "Lam Che Village, Lantau Island (Hiding Place of Members of the Lantau Detachment of the Hong Kong-Kowloon Brigade)",
        "paras":  [
                      "Lam Che Village is located near the old fort of Tung Chung on Lantau Island, close to Nim Yuen and Shek Lau Po Village. In May 1944, the Japanese troops launched a large-scale \"mopping-up\" operation on Lantau Island. With the villagers\u0027 support, Chen Shaoming, a civilian mobilisation worker, and Mo Qingyou, a messenger, both of the Lantau Detachment, hid in a cave here for more than ten days. Ah Niu\u0027s wife from Shek Lau Po Village and Auntie Ah Ji from Lam Che Village risked their lives to bring the two men military intelligence and food. This allowed them to hold out until the Japanese troops withdrew and to return safely to their unit."
                  ]
