        "title":  "Historic Site of Kwong Kee Fresh and Salted Fish Store (A Transit Point of the Secret Rescue Operation)",
        "subtitle":  "A Transit Point of the Secret Rescue Operation",
        "listName":  "Historic Site of Kwong Kee Fresh and Salted Fish Store (A Transit Point of the Secret Rescue Operation)",
        "paras":  [
                      "Cheung Chau was a transit point on the sea route of the Secret Rescue Operation. Many democrats and renowned cultural figures left Hong Kong by sea for Macao via Cheung Chau. On 9 January 1942, 21 people, including the cultural figures Xia Yan, Jin Zhonghua, Situ Huimin, Cai Chusheng and his wife Chen Manyun, set off from Sai Wan on Hong Kong Island. They spent a night at Kwong Kee Fresh and Salted Fish Store on Cheung Chau and reached Macao the next afternoon. They then travelled on through Zhongshan, Taishan and other places to Guilin in Guangxi. On 11 January, nine cultural figures, including Hua Jia and Xie Jiayin, set off from Sai Ying Pun on Hong Kong Island. After reaching Cheung Chau, they stayed at Kwong Kee Fresh and Salted Fish Store for three days before going on to Macao. Both groups sailed from Cheung Chau and reached Macao safely on the same day."
                  ]
