        "image":  "assets/img/40.jpg",
        "source":  "https://hk.waranddefence.museum/en/web/mcd/interactive-map-40.html",
        "name":  "Historic Site of Sang Lung Tai Incense Factory",
        "title":  "Historic Site of Sang Lung Tai Incense Factory (A Transit Point in the Secret Rescue Operation)",
        "subtitle":  "A Transit Point in the Secret Rescue Operation",
        "listName":  "Historic Site of Sang Lung Tai Incense Factory (A Transit Point in the Secret Rescue Operation)",
        "paras":  [
                      "During the Secret Rescue Operation, Li Shaoshi and his wife Liao Mengxing travelled to Macao via Cheung Chau. Li Shaoshi was an operative sent to Hong Kong directly by Zhou Enlai. Liao Mengxing, the daughter of He Xiangning, worked at the China Defence League led by Soong Ching-ling. In late January 1942, Pan Jing\u0027an, a confidential cadre of the Eighth Route Army Hong Kong Office, brought the couple to Cheung Chau and handed them over to Chen Liangming, an underground Party member, who was to take them to Macao. Because the Japanese army had blockaded the waters near Cheung Chau and the wind was against them, they had to stay on Cheung Chau for a while. They lodged at the home of Su Huizhen, the proprietress of the Sang Lung Tai Incense Factory. After staying for more than 20 days, they finally had a favourable tide and wind, and Chen Liangming and his brother took the couple to Macao."
                  ]
