        "title":  "102 Hollywood Road (Historic Site of the Hua Shang Daily)",
        "subtitle":  "Historic Site of the Hua Shang Daily",
        "listName":  "102 Hollywood Road (Historic Site of the Hua Shang Daily)",
        "paras":  [
                      "The Hua Shang Daily was first published on 8 April 1941. Its office was at 102 Hollywood Road, Hong Kong Island, and it was led by Liao Chengzhi, the director of the Eighth Route Army Hong Kong Office. After its launch, the newspaper actively promoted the Anti-Japanese National United Front of the Communist Party of China. It publicised the achievements of the Eighth Route Army, the New Fourth Army and the South China anti-Japanese guerrillas in the War of Resistance, and exposed the crimes of Japanese imperialism in its invasion of China. On 12 December 1941, the Hua Shang Daily stopped publication because of the Japanese invasion of Hong Kong.",
                      "After victory in the War of Resistance, the Hua Shang Daily resumed publication on 4 January 1946 and became a patriotic newspaper with great influence in South China and overseas. After the liberation of Guangzhou in October 1949, the Hua Shang Daily stopped publication, and its staff moved to Guangzhou to found the Nanfang Daily."
                  ]
