        "listName":  "300 Lai Chi Kok Road (Historic Site of Nanhua Pharmacy, a Secret Liaison Point of the Eighth Route Army Hong Kong Office)",
        "paras":  [
                      "In August 1929, Ke Lin withdrew from Shanghai to Hong Kong. With the help of his younger brother Ke Ping and his parents, he opened the Nanhua Pharmacy at 300 Lai Chi Kok Road, Sham Shui Po, Kowloon. He practised medicine under the name “Chinese medicine practitioner Ke Lin” as a cover for the underground intelligence and liaison work of the Communist Party of China. When the Eighth Route Army Hong Kong Office was set up in January 1938, the Nanhua Pharmacy continued to serve as a secret liaison point."
                  ]
