                      "Pun Uk, also known as the Mansion of Yum Wah, is located at Au Tau, Yuen Long. It was built by the merchant Pun Kwan-min in the 1930s. In November 1938, while Ye Jianying, the Chief of Staff of the Eighth Route Army, was receiving medical treatment in Hong Kong, he was invited to Pun Uk as a guest. Inspired by Ye Jianying, Pun Kwan-min mobilised the Hong Kong business community to donate money in support of the War of Resistance. Through Ye Jianying, he also sent two of his nephews to join the Eighth Route Army.",
