                      "Shan Ha Tsuen, part of Ping Shan Heung, is a village in Yuen Long District in the New Territories. During the War of Resistance, the Yuen Long Detachment of the Hong Kong-Kowloon Brigade held meetings in two study halls in the village. The two study halls stood in an inner lane close to the hillside, so the guerrillas could escape quickly when necessary. The Hong Kong-Kowloon Brigade\u0027s civilian mobilisation workers in Yuen Long District organised five guerrilla groups, and the group at Shan Ha Tsuen had the most members. In January 1945, villager Zhang Jinfu was tortured to death by the Japanese army for protecting the guerrilla Chen Rui. He gave his young life."
